OL,3,GNEWSAParking charges would drive
OL,4,Ashoppers away, businesses fear
OL,5,
OL,6,FParking charges would be a "nail in the
OL,7,Fcoffin for us", says Julie Wooley. The
OL,8,F59-year-old works in Ossett and fears
OL,9,Fthe planned scrapping of a parking
OL,10,Fscheme across the Wakefield borough
OL,11,Fwould be detrimental for the town.
OL,13,F"We have really good markets and it
OL,14,Fbrings people in, but if you scrap the
OL,15,Ffree parking, people will go to big
OL,16,Fplaces like Trinity Walk and White
OL,17,FRose," she says.
OL,19,FReform UK councillors are proposing to
OL,20,Fcut a current two-hour free parking
OL,21,Fconcession.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
